  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "IMI-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-isogeny-dvr-target",
      "title": "A polarized isogeny out of an integral marked object has an integral target",
      "hypotheses": "Let q be prime, N ≥ 3 prime to q, and V a discrete valuation ring mapping to the Harris–Taylor PEL base, with fraction field K. All integers prime to q are units in V. The integral model uses a characteristic-zero base DVR R with q in its maximal ideal. The marked object over V has generic fibre admitting a polarized isogeny of multiplier c=q^e, a compatible level and order action, and a companion whose two composites are [c].",
      "statement": "The marked generic target extends over V. Its abelian scheme is the quotient by the finite flat schematic closure of the generic kernel, and the isogeny extends with its multiplier. A test extending s₀(x) thus admits an extension of t₀(x). For the reverse lifting test, if B extends, the companion S_f B → A extends the original source A, with q^{e+f} ≡ 1 mod N.",
      "definitions": [
        "Flatness of the schematic closure over V and its inclusion in finite A[c] give a finite flat subgroup.",
        "S_a changes the level marking η to the marking x ↦ η(q^a x) on the same object."
      ],
