      "title": "Reducedness of the normal model",
      "hypotheses": "The base R is a characteristic-zero DVR with q in its maximal ideal, X is smooth over R, and the source map of the generic correspondence Y₀ is étale over X[1/q]. The integral model Y is flat over R and the inclusion of Y₀ identifies the locus where q is invertible.",
      "statement": "Every nilpotent on an affine open of Y vanishes, so Y is reduced.",
